            "currentUpdate": "Tessa Lane's operative record describes elective mesh abdominal-wall repair without bowel entry or infected tissue. Cefazolin was first given before incision, repeated during the operation and then carried onto the discharge medication list. She now has an intact incision, expected mild tenderness, no spreading erythema and no fever. A drain retained for a postoperative seroma has been present since surgery. A specimen from its disinfected port now reports MSSA susceptible to cefazolin and cephalexin; no new cavity was accessed. Wound and drain reassessment will continue with every medication plan.",
