            "primaryConceptId": "concept.pancreas-acute-pancreatitis.refractory-compartment-decompression.v1",
            "currentUpdate": "Repeated standardized bladder-pressure measurements were 28 and 30 mmHg. Sedation, paralysis and nasogastric/rectal decompression had been optimized. A percutaneous catheter drained the accessible ascites, but pressure and renal/ventilatory dysfunction persisted; the repeat study showed only a small residual fluid layer. Necrosis remained early and unencapsulated, without evidence of infection.",
