            "currentUpdate": "Contrast injection through both flank catheters filled the liquid spaces around the residual material, and both catheters flushed freely. Follow-up CT showed collapse of those liquid spaces around the drains but little change in the bulky nonliquid component. Fever and organ-support needs persisted despite susceptibility-active antibiotics. The flank catheter tips lay beside the residual burden; colon still separated the collection from the stomach.",
