        "learningSummary": "Failed therapy and the ongoing acute steroid/nutritional burden determine the operative phase. Total abdominal colectomy with end ileostomy controls the colonic disease while deferring rectal dissection and reconstruction. Total proctocolectomy with a permanent stoma avoids a pouch anastomosis but still adds pelvic surgery now. Diversion also does not remove the risks of immediate pouch construction."
