                "label": "Stop argatroban and resume UFH prophylaxis",
                "isCorrect": true,
                "rationale": "The delayed platelet course justified initial suspected-HIT treatment, but weak binding positivity does not establish pathogenic HIT antibodies. A valid negative functional result changes that assessment: most such patients do not have HIT and can be managed accordingly, including heparin if it remains indicated. Functional tests can be falsely negative, especially with a high-probability course and strongly positive immunoassay. The weak binding result here does not supply that strong-immunoassay conflict; clinical reassessment remains necessary.",
