        "learningSummary": "With cosyntropin, the right and left cortisol selectivity ratios are 10 and 20. The corrected aldosterone ratios are 1200/200 = 6 and 2400/400 = 6, so the larger left raw value does not show lateralization. Use a mineralocorticoid receptor antagonist with potassium and renal monitoring rather than operate on the CT nodule or repeat an adequate study."
