            "currentUpdate": "{patientName} has a primary reducing inguinal hernia that limits walking. He remains active without a cardiopulmonary limitation and follows instructions throughout the supine examination. An earlier prostate-cancer operative note describes dissection behind the pubic bone to the prostatic apex and creation of a vesicourethral anastomosis. The consulting surgeons regularly perform the offered repair and anesthesia combinations.",
