    "learningSummary": "Read the separate measurements for their separate purposes. The integrated post-sequence contraction, rather than its peak alone, is the reserve comparison. The baseline waves show propagation, and the junction trace during liquid loading does not support impaired relaxation. Report reduced reserve with preserved relaxation. The common timed-esophagram request assesses actual emptying; this question does not claim that a reserve result selects barium over every other investigation or proves the cause of dysphagia. The failed/premature body activity with impaired junction relaxation is an achalasia-like spastic pattern. Opioids can produce this phenotype; Chicago v4 advises studying off opioids when possible. Coordinate a clinically appropriate withdrawal/reassessment plan before treating this as established primary disease requiring myotomy. No abrupt cessation or fixed washout is prescribed."
